<content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>


<para>A framed picture has a total area \(y\), in square inches. The thickness of the frame is represented by \(x\), in inches. The equation \(y = (2x + 8)(2x + 10)\) relates these two variables.</para>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What is the width, or shorter side, of the picture without the frame?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter the width.</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> 8 inches</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What is the length, or longer side, of the picture without the frame?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter the length.</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> 10 inches</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What would a solution to the equation \(100 = (2x + 8)(2x + 10)\) mean in this situation?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your explanation.</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> The solution would represent the thickness of a frame that results in a total area of 100 square inches.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End --></section>
</content>
